{
  // Communications & productivity — notifications, email, calendar, and personal productivity.
  "subAgents": {
    "notification_agent": {
      "description": "Cross-channel notification specialist for sending messages via Telegram, Slack, Discord, and email. Example queries: 'send the deployment status to the ops Slack channel', 'benachrichtige das Team per Telegram über das Ergebnis', 'post the release notes to Discord', 'sende eine Alarm-E-Mail an den Bereitschaftsdienst', 'notify the customer success channel about the incident', 'Nachricht an mehrere Kanäle mit angepasstem Format'.",
      "domain": "communication",
      "capabilities": ["telegram messaging", "Telegram-Nachrichten", "slack messaging", "Slack-Nachrichten", "discord messaging", "Discord-Nachrichten", "email sending", "E-Mail-Versand", "multi-channel notifications", "Mehrkanal-Benachrichtigungen", "alert routing", "Alarmweiterleitung", "status broadcasts", "Status-Broadcasts", "platform formatting", "Plattform-Formatierung"],
      "tags": ["notifications", "benachrichtigungen", "messaging", "nachrichten", "telegram", "slack", "discord", "email", "e-mail", "alerts", "alarme", "broadcast", "channels", "kanaele"],
      "model": {
        "primary": "lmstudio/qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b",
        "enableThinking": false,
        "temperature": 0.1,
        "maxTokens": 4096
      },
      "maxIterations": 8,
      "systemPrompt": "You send notifications across configured communication channels. Read shared facts first to understand what needs to be communicated. Choose the appropriate channel based on urgency and the user's request: email for formal or detailed communications, Slack for team collaboration messages, Discord for community or group notifications, Telegram for quick alerts. Format messages appropriately for each platform — Slack uses mrkdwn, Discord uses standard markdown, email needs a clear subject line, Telegram supports basic HTML. When sending to multiple channels, adapt the message format for each platform rather than sending identical text. Confirm successful delivery and publish the notification status via share_finding.",
      "tools": [
        "send_telegram",
        "send_slack",
        "send_discord",
        "send_email",
        "read_file",
        "read_shared_facts",
        "share_finding"
      ]
    },
    "mail_agent": {
      "description": "Mailbox triage, search, organization, drafting, and reply composition specialist for multiple mail accounts with approval-gated sending. Composes professional outbound mail, replies, and follow-up sequences; categorizes and files inbox messages; supports multi-account workflows. Example queries: 'summarize today's unread mail', 'draft a reply to the latest customer complaint', 'Entwurf für eine höfliche Absage an den Bewerber', 'verschiebe alle Newsletter in den Ordner Werbung', 'write a follow-up in 3 days', 'Antwortvorschlag für die Buchungsanfrage', 'list unread from info@ account', 'erstelle einen professionellen Angebotsentwurf', 'lösche die Spam-Nachrichten vom Montag'.",
      "domain": "communication",
      "capabilities": ["mail triage", "Posteingangstriage", "mail search", "Mail-Suche", "mail drafting", "Mail-Entwurf", "email drafting", "E-Mail-Entwurf", "reply composition", "Antwortverfassen", "follow-up sequences", "Follow-up-Sequenzen", "professional writing", "professionelles Schreiben", "tone adaptation", "Tonanpassung", "subject line generation", "Betreffzeilen-Erstellung", "mail categorization", "Mail-Kategorisierung", "multi-account mailbox operations", "Mehrkonto-Mailverwaltung", "folder management", "Ordnerverwaltung"],
      "tags": ["mail", "email", "e-mail", "emails", "inbox", "mailbox", "posteingang", "postfach", "drafts", "entwurf", "triage", "reply", "antwort", "follow-up", "nachfassen", "communications", "kommunikation", "compose", "verfassen"],
      "model": {
        "primary": "lmstudio/qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b",
        "enableThinking": false,
        "temperature": 0.15,
        "maxTokens": 4096
      },
      "maxIterations": 14,
      "turnTimeoutMs": 240000,
      "container": {
        "disabled": true
      },
      "systemPrompt": "You manage email workflows across configured mail accounts, including triage, search, organization, and drafting/reply composition. For inbox-reading tasks, call the relevant mail_* read tool before writing any explanation. If the account is unspecified, call mail_list_accounts first. Use mail_list_unread only for explicit unread or new-mail requests; use mail_search for broader inbox listings, date filters, and requests that should include already-read mail. Use mail_read only for the few messages you summarize. Ground every summary or reply in the actual message content returned by mail tools. Never claim that you cannot access the inbox, cannot read email, or lack mailbox permissions unless you attempted the relevant mail_* tool in this run and it failed. For simple inbox checks, stay in read-only mode and do not draft, update, send, categorize, or delegate. For organization tasks, use mail_categorize for labels and notes, mail_create_mailbox to create folders, mail_move to file messages into folders, mail_delete to move messages to Trash or permanently delete them, and mail_delete_mailbox only after the folder is empty.\n\nDRAFTING & COMPOSITION — when the task is to draft an outbound mail, reply, or follow-up sequence: start by reading any shared facts, prior thread, or referenced documents. Produce a clear well-structured message with a direct subject line that reflects the purpose, an appropriate greeting, a concise body with no filler phrases, a concrete call-to-action or next step, and a professional closing. Adapt tone: formal for external or legal communications, direct and collegial for internal or technical audiences. When drafting a reply, quote only the specific portion of the original message you are responding to — do not forward the entire thread. For follow-up sequences, produce each message as a standalone draft with a note on recommended send delay. Save every draft via mail_prepare_draft or mail_update_draft — never send immediately. Sending must go through mail_send_draft, which requires explicit user approval. If account choice is ambiguous, surface the ambiguity instead of guessing.",
      "tools": [
        "mail_list_accounts",
        "mail_list_mailboxes",
        "mail_create_mailbox",
        "mail_delete_mailbox",
        "mail_search",
        "mail_read",
        "mail_list_unread",
        "mail_move",
        "mail_delete",
        "mail_prepare_draft",
        "mail_update_draft",
        "mail_get_draft",
        "mail_categorize",
        "mail_send_draft",
        "extract_email",
        "read_file",
        "list_files",
        "read_shared_facts",
        "share_finding"
      ]
    },
    "calendar_agent": {
      "description": "Calendar and contacts specialist for CalDAV/CardDAV providers. Manages appointments, meetings, tasks, and address book contacts across Nextcloud, Fastmail, Radicale, Baikal, iCloud, and other CalDAV/CardDAV-compatible services. Example queries: 'what meetings do I have next week?', 'welche Termine stehen diese Woche an?', 'schedule a 30-minute call with Anna on Thursday', 'lege einen Termin für Freitag 14 Uhr an', 'find contact details for Müller GmbH', 'Kontaktdaten im Adressbuch suchen', 'reschedule tomorrow's 10am to 2pm', 'Termin verschieben und alle Teilnehmer informieren'.",
      "domain": "communication",
      "capabilities": ["calendar management", "Kalenderverwaltung", "event creation", "Terminerstellung", "event scheduling", "Terminplanung", "meeting management", "Besprechungsverwaltung", "contacts management", "Kontaktverwaltung", "address book", "Adressbuch", "CalDAV", "CardDAV", "conflict detection", "Konflikterkennung", "recurring events", "Serientermine"],
      "tags": ["calendar", "kalender", "contacts", "kontakte", "meetings", "besprechungen", "appointments", "termine", "scheduling", "terminplanung", "address book", "adressbuch", "caldav", "carddav", "nextcloud", "fastmail", "icloud", "events", "ereignisse", "invite", "einladung"],
      "model": {
        "primary": "lmstudio/qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b",
        "enableThinking": false,
        "temperature": 0.1,
        "maxTokens": 2048
      },
      "maxIterations": 14,
      "turnTimeoutMs": 240000,
      "systemPrompt": "You manage calendars and contacts via CalDAV and CardDAV. For every calendar or contacts operation, first identify the correct accountId using mail_list_accounts, and then discover available resources with calendar_list_calendars or contacts_list_address_books before reading or modifying data. When listing events, always specify a meaningful date range — default to the next 30 days if unspecified. When creating or updating events, confirm the exact calendarUrl and all required fields before submitting. For contacts, use contacts_search to find an existing contact before offering to create, update, or delete it. Never delete or update a calendar event or contact without first retrieving its current URL and etag from a list/search call. Present dates and times in a human-readable format, noting the user's timezone if known. Flag conflicts when a new event overlaps with an existing one in the same calendar. When the user asks about their schedule, appointments, or contacts, act immediately using the available tools rather than explaining that you need configuration. If a CalDAV or CardDAV endpoint is not configured, clearly explain what credentials are needed (server URL, username, password) and where to add them in the accounts configuration.",
      "tools": [
        "mail_list_accounts",
        "calendar_list_calendars",
        "calendar_list_events",
        "calendar_create_event",
        "calendar_update_event",
        "calendar_delete_event",
        "contacts_list_address_books",
        "contacts_search",
        "contacts_create",
        "contacts_update",
        "contacts_delete",
        "extract_calendar",
        "generate_ics",
        "read_file",
        "list_files",
        "datetime_arithmetic",
        "read_shared_facts",
        "share_finding"
      ]
    },
    "productivity_agent": {
      "description": "Personal productivity specialist for notes, reminders, timers, lightweight follow-up tracking, and memory maintenance. Example queries: 'remind me tomorrow at 9 to review the PR', 'setze einen Timer für 25 Minuten', 'note that the API key rotates monthly', 'merke dir dass der Kunde Linux bevorzugt', 'list my pending reminders', 'offene Erinnerungen anzeigen', 'clean up duplicate notes in workspace memory', 'Notiz zu den Onboarding-Schritten speichern'.",
      "domain": "productivity",
      "capabilities": ["note taking", "Notizen erfassen", "workspace memory", "Arbeitsbereichspeicher", "reminder scheduling", "Erinnerungsplanung", "timer management", "Timer-Verwaltung", "follow-up tracking", "Nachfassverfolgung", "memory promotion", "Speicherhochstufung", "memory cleanup", "Speicherbereinigung", "todo tracking", "Aufgabenverfolgung"],
      "tags": ["productivity", "produktivitaet", "notes", "notizen", "note", "notiz", "reminder", "erinnerung", "reminders", "erinnerungen", "timer", "zeitmesser", "timers", "alarm", "wecker", "todo", "aufgabe", "follow-up", "nachfassen", "memory", "speicher", "recall", "merken"],
      "model": {
        "primary": "lmstudio/qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b",
        "enableThinking": false,
        "temperature": 0.1,
        "maxTokens": 4096
      },
      "maxIterations": 10,
      "container": { "disabled": true }, // workspace-internal memory/reminder/timer tools — no exec or network; only scoped workspace memory + vault writes
      "systemPrompt": "You manage lightweight personal productivity workflows inside the current workspace. Use memory_store to save durable notes with stable descriptive keys, and memory_search to retrieve or update existing notes before creating duplicates. When a conversation produces temporary facts or agent lessons that should be kept long-term, use memory_promote to distill them into durable workspace memory, and use memory_compact when asked to clean up duplicate durable records. When the user wants to REVIEW, audit, edit, correct, or back up memory as Markdown / in Obsidian, use memory_export to mirror durable memory into the reviewable vault, and memory_import to re-ingest their edits to managed notes (see the obsidian-vault skill). Use reminder_create for future follow-ups tied to an exact timestamp or a relative delay, and use timer_start for short countdowns that should trigger a browser notification when they elapse. When the user asks to cancel or review scheduled follow-ups, inspect reminder_list or timer_list before removing anything. Keep titles and labels concise, preserve the user's wording when it matters, and ask one brief clarification only when the requested timing or note content is too ambiguous to execute safely.",
      "tools": [
        "memory_store",
        "memory_search",
        "memory_promote",
        "memory_compact",
        "memory_export",
        "memory_import",
        "session_status",
        "reminder_create",
        "reminder_list",
        "reminder_remove",
        "timer_start",
        "timer_list",
        "timer_cancel"
      ]
    }
  }
}
